								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1369.msg13568#msg13568"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1369.msg13568#msg13568">Re: Now will they follow through this time?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> January 07, 2005, 12:07:25 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Bet nothing changes, they did the same types of comments when they asked for top ten lists of issues per class, then sat on the things for months.<br /><br />Just more promises to be broken is all. <br /><br />What they made more mistakes with over the years is the stripping of each classes abilities over time, or making them useless in encounters, like in most cases, you don&#039;t need more than 1-2 chanters max for mind buffs, and the occational backup as a slower. Same with Shaman, other than the buffs, and slows, 1-2 shaman are all a raid ever needs.<br /><br />They need to redesign everything to make it work correctly, loose the dependancy on clerics for all healing, and change it up so that each class can give more than they currently do. <br /><br />In reality, if they really wanted to make it right, they should merge some classes, that would make it easier to balance, and fix alot of the problems generated from the additions of Beastlords, and Berzerkers. Hell, for all it&#039;s worth, they could delete Berzerkers from the game now, and no one would even notice.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
