	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13730"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 398<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1369.msg13730#msg13730"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1369.msg13730#msg13730">Re: Now will they follow through this time?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> January 17, 2005, 09:39:24 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Eh, you&#039;ve got what, 16 classes now?&nbsp; It&#039;s too many IMO and EQ2 is going with even more classes.&nbsp; The biggest problem is EQ1 though is the model of 1 mob versus a group.&nbsp; Most areas and their mobs are still designed around a massive dps mob that will be single pulled or reduced to a single by crowd control.&nbsp; So you&#039;ve got 1 mob on the tank and everyone else filling a few roles to take it down and keep the tank up.&nbsp; It severely limits what sorts of contributions will be useful.&nbsp; I don&#039;t see that ever changing significantly in EQ1 though.&nbsp; The entire system is designed around it now.&nbsp; Given that ugly restriction, classes aren&#039;t in too bad of shape balance wise and a major overhaul would probably just screw up more than it fixes. <br /><br />Besides, it&#039;s hard to feel like a hero when most of the mobs you fight at high levels are much stronger than any one of your characters.&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/razz.gif" alt="Razz" border="0" /> I just got depressed as a tank encountering things like &quot;flies&quot; in GoD that hit for over 1k, or goblins back in ldon that can hit for over 900 while I&#039;m thwacking away at them for about 50 to 125 a pop.&nbsp; Bah... the goblin is the hero there, valiantly defending his cave against half a dozen nasty invading characters.&nbsp; &nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
